  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Side event at ICC Assembly of States Parties on working towards standards on integration of MHPSS in accountability mechanisms for atrocity crimes</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Next step in promoting integration of Mental Health and Psychosocial Support in accountability mechanisms for atrocity crimes (recommendations developed with funding from Knowledge Management Fund of KPSRL) is organising a side event at the Assembly of States Parties of the ICC on the development of standards to this effect. Side event is during lunch hour. Providing luncheon can only be done through services of World Forum at cost of EUR 33 p.p. Room provides space for 51 persons (amounting to almost EUR 2,000). One or two speakers will join virtually, for which additional technical means and support are required @ EUR 115. Finally, one speaker (Syrian refugee, survivor, lived experience) may travel in from Germany by train, for which a budget is reserved of EUR   235.</narrative>
  </description>
